  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "A contest began at noon one day and ended \\(1000\\) minutes later. At what time did the contest end?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\!:\\!00\\) p.m.",
    "B": "midnight",
    "C": "\\(2\\!:\\!30\\) a.m.",
    "D": "\\(4\\!:\\!40\\) a.m.",
    "E": "\\(6\\!:\\!40\\) a.m."
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Use midnight as a stopping point, since it is \\(12\\) hours after noon. With \\(60\\) minutes in an hour, reaching midnight uses\n\\[\n12\\times60=720\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nThe time remaining after midnight is\n\\[\n1000-720=280\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nSince \\(280=4\\times60+40\\), the contest continues for another \\(4\\) hours and \\(40\\) minutes after midnight. It therefore ends at \\(\\boxed{4\\!:\\!40\\text{ a.m.}}\\) the next day, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
